---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Refund policy"
  description="Final Commit's refund policy: you pay per stage after each stage is done, nothing before your guide approves the synopsis."
  updated="7 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    You pay for each stage only after that stage is done, so most of the time there is nothing to refund. These are the cases where
    money comes back to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Before your guide approves the synopsis</h2>
  <p>
    You haven't paid anything. If your guide rejects the topic, we rework it with you, or you can walk away owing nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>If we can't deliver a stage</h2>
  <p>
    If we can't deliver a stage, you don't pay for it. If you've already paid for it, we refund that payment in full within 7 working
    days, to the same UPI ID or bank account it came from.
  </p>

  <h2>If we miss an agreed date</h2>
  <p>
    If we miss a date in your written quote, and you had sent us what we needed on time, you can stop there. You keep everything
    delivered so far, and you don't pay for the stages that are left.
  </p>

  <h2>If you decide to stop</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop at any point. Stages that are already delivered and paid for aren't refunded, and you don't pay for anything that
    hasn't been delivered yet.
  </p>

  <h2>How to ask for a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Message us on WhatsApp at {site.phone} or email {site.email} with your name and the payment receipt. We confirm within one working
    day.
  </p>
</Legal>
